ry'>He denies having kidney stones before,</span> <span style='color:#673AB7; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Personal History</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#EF6C00;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Family History'>but states that his father has a history of kidney stones in the past.</span> <span style='color:#EF6C00; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Family History</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#C2185B;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Acute Symptoms'>He explains that when he had pain, which has now resolved, it would radiate almost to his groin.</span> <span style='color:#C2185B; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Acute Symptoms</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#C2185B;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Acute Symptoms'>The patient describes the pain as intermittent after he found out it was a kidney stone</span> <span style='color:#C2185B; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Acute Symptoms</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#303F9F;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Theraputic History'>He explains that he has been straining his urine, but has not seen anything.</span> <span style='color:#303F9F; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Theraputic History</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#E91E63;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Vegetative History'>He denies any hematuria.</span> <span style='color:#E91E63; font-size:14px;'>(<b>Vegetative History</b>)</span></li><li><span style='color:#E91E63;' data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' title='Vegetative History'>REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

